## 2. Environment Updates

### Root `package.json` Improvements
The root `package.json` file orchestrates the entire monolithic structure (frontend, backend, and AI service).

A new command has been added to make future health checks easier:
```json
"scripts": {
    "lint": "npm run lint --prefix frontend"
}
```
You can now run `npm run lint` directly from the main project directory (`c:\Users\HP\Desktop\PlantCare`) to instantly check the health of the React frontend.

### Port Conflicts & Cleanup
Due to multiple concurrent runs of `npm run dev`, some Node.js and Python processes were left stranded in the background, specifically locking up:
*   **Port 3000** (React Frontend)
*   **Port 5000** (Python AI Service)
*   **Port 8000** (Node.js Backend)

These processes caused `EADDRINUSE` crashes. To resolve this, a forceful termination of tasks utilizing these ports was initiated.

> [!TIP]
> If you experience `EADDRINUSE` errors again in the future, you can execute the included **`fix-ports.bat`** script by double-clicking it or typing `.\fix-ports.bat` in your terminal. This will automatically clear ports 3000, 5000, and 8000 for you.

